WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.100
Here's the path on one page, each step
with a done-when and a way to validate it.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.899
One: protect the hierarchy,
assign the security initiative,

3
00:00:08.899 --> 00:00:10.837
and get platform logs flowing.

4
00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:14.177
Two: put every public I P,
Front Door endpoint and

5
00:00:14.177 --> 00:00:17.601
application gateway in a
register with an owner.

6
00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.957
Three: DDoS protection
on every public I P,

7
00:00:20.957 --> 00:00:24.412
logged and alerting,
with one exercise run.

8
00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:27.851
Four: the web application
firewall in prevention mode.

9
00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:31.114
Five: origins that only
the edge can reach,

10
00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:34.762
T L S one point two at
least, and failover tested.

11
00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:37.258
Six: default routes to Azure Firewall,

12
00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:41.201
with threat intelligence and
intrusion detection in deny.

13
00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:44.326
Seven: platform services
with public access off,

14
00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:47.062
resolving through central private zones.

15
00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:50.750
Eight: vaults on role-based
access with purge protection.

16
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.725
Nine: policy that holds it,
with exemptions that expire.

17
00:00:54.725 --> 00:00:57.875
Ten: owners, cadence and evidence.

18
00:00:57.875 --> 00:01:03.070
Steps one and two come first; three to
eight can run in parallel by workload.
